=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network described in ticket #9009 is operating correctly at the time of
investigation. End-to-end connectivity from pc1 (195.11.14.2) to pc2
(200.1.1.2) is fully functional with zero packet loss. The BGP session
between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) over the 193.10.11.0/24 link is
ESTABLISHED and stable. Router1's FIB contains 200.1.1.0/24 learned via
eBGP from router2, and router2's FIB contains 195.11.14.0/24 learned from
router1. Neither router has any prefix-list, route-map, or inbound/outbound
filter configured — the BGP configuration on both sides is minimal and
correct, with only the local network statement and the remote-as peer
declaration.

The BGP log entries showing "DENIED due to: as-path contains our own AS" are
normal loop-prevention behavior: each router re-advertises learned routes back
to the originating AS, which correctly rejects them. The single "BGP OPEN
receipt failed" entry on router2 is a standard connection-collision event
during simultaneous BGP startup, not a fault — the session resolved and has
been stable since.

The lab appears to have started only a few minutes before the investigation
began. The most likely explanation for the reported outage is that the lab
(and therefore BGP) had not yet started or had been recently restarted when
the user submitted the ticket. The symptom had already self-resolved by the
time of inspection. No corrective action is required; the network is healthy.
=== END ===
